# `Dockerfile` ends in `COPY . .`, so anything listed here is something that must not become part
# of an image. `.env` is first for that reason: an image carrying real credentials leaks them to
# anyone who can pull or inspect it, and the running container gets its configuration from the
# environment instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

tests/
*.sqlite
*.db
